import "core"
import "process/page.ct"
import "process/findReplace.ct"


module(Process)
  # # Processing a page
    `catln process` runs the processors of the annotations written on a page, top to bottom. There
    are two kinds:
    - A line processor, an arm of `/Catln/process{io}(annot)`, updates its annotation and nothing
      else, as a [/Llm/#q] is answered.
    - A file processor, an arm of `/Catln/processFile{io}(annot, page, annotId)`, gives the page it
      is written on as it is to become, or why it can not be ([/Data/Result]). It is given the page
      as a [/Catln/RawPrgm], and the ID of its own annotation in it as `annotId`. Where it changes
      the page, the page is written, compiled again and processed again from the top, until a pass
      over the page changes nothing.
    This is not part of the standard library, and a page using its processors writes
    `import "process"`.
    It is written in parts, each a page of this directory:
    - @process/page.ct@ is what a page is rewritten with: [setAnnot], [removeAnnot], [formatPage]
      and [parsePage].
    - @process/findReplace.ct@ is [#findReplace], replacing text throughout a page.
